  "worked_solution": "Since the straight angle must have a measure of ${180}^{\u2218},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m\u2220HAC+m\u2220BAC & ={180}^{\u2218} \\\\ m\u2220HAC+{110}^{\u2218} & ={180}^{\u2218} \\\\ m\u2220HAC & ={70}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\u25b3ACH$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to ${180}^{\u2218},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m\u2220HCA+m\u2220HAC+m\u2220AHC & ={180}^{\u2218} \\\\ m\u2220HCA+{70}^{\u2218}+{90}^{\u2218} & ={180}^{\u2218} \\\\ m\u2220HCA+{160}^{\u2218} & ={180}^{\u2218} \\\\ m\u2220HCA & ={20}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
